---
import { systemGuidelines } from '../data/system-guidelines';
const { contrasts, outline, offset, target } = systemGuidelines();
---
<section id="accessibility" class="ds-section"><header class="ds-heading"><h2>Accessibility</h2></header>
  <ul class="ds-guidance">
    <li>Use the primary and secondary text roles for readable copy; check accent text against its size and background.</li>
    <li>Keep the shared focus outline: <code>{outline}</code>, with <code>{offset}</code> offset.</li>
    <li>Keep control targets at least <code>{target} × {target}</code>. Inline prose links retain their inline treatment.</li>
    <li>Use named native controls and preserve keyboard order. Closing a case study returns focus to its project card.</li>
    <li>Keep meaningful image alternatives and video controls with the media.</li>
    <li>Respect reduced motion: content stays available, repeated decoration stops, and case studies open without travel.</li>
  </ul>
  <details class="ds-all-tokens"><summary>Source-computed contrast</summary><div class="ds-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Text / background</th><th>Light</th><th>Dark</th></tr></thead><tbody>{contrasts.map(pair => <tr><th><code>{pair.foreground}</code><br /><code>{pair.background}</code></th>{pair.themes.map(result => <td>{result.ratio}:1 · {result.normalTextAA ? 'AA for normal text' : 'Below AA for normal text'}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details>
</section>
<section id="writing" class="ds-section"><header class="ds-heading"><h2>Writing</h2></header>
  <ul class="ds-guidance"><li>Name the destination or action. Case-study project links use “Website”.</li><li>Keep project names, outcomes and supplied claims in their original context.</li><li>Keep the supplied dates and durations; do not calculate new timeline copy.</li><li>Keep supporting notes with their metrics. Do not turn a supplied claim into a measured result.</li><li>Use the supplied tool names as accessible labels. Do not add captions or slogans.</li></ul>
</section>
